Not only a question of conduct - I am interested in what you think...

It was, AFAIR, the first time that I found Orcus' level rather empty,
no Orcus, no shades (well, some 4's are cowardly hiding behind some
wall, maybe that's the rest of them), no skeletons; really abandoned.
Just a lonely ghost that tries to protect his loot that was dropped
by his former incarnation on the down staircase.[*]

The poor heroe's loot contained some interesting stuff; a cursed
magic lamp (I had not yet got permanent light), a cursed wand (which
I hope will turn out to be Orcus' wand), and in the blessed bag of
holding there is... The Eye of the Aethiopica.

Usually I have no qualms taking everything, but I am very reluctant
to take that artifact (since I don't wish for artifacts, as a matter
of principle). Besides my scruple I am not sure whether I could use
it at all; The Eye is an intelligent artifact, and it is neutral as
my Priest is.

Could I pick it up?  Get the carry bonus?  Be able to #invoke it?

Sure, it's not like wishing for artifacts, but somewhat cheap... :-/
Never mind, I think I'll take it with me, _if_ it works. :-}

Janis

